{1030}{To P. Schuyler & Sons
}
{1031}{Please accept this telegram as my commitment for payment of the signet ring I had made for my son, Gilbert Bates.
}
{1032}{Payment has been wired as per your instructions.  I will arrive in Tarant in two weeks to pick up the ring.
}
{1033}{Sincerely,

Benjamin Bates}

{1040}{I have discovered something interesting concerning our "friends" with the strange amulets.}
{1041}{I am off to investigate my theories regarding them, please accept my humblest apologies on my inability to meet with you in Tarant.}
{1042}{I understand all of this must be a bit disconcerting, for both of you.  If you've questions concerning the Panarii religion, stop by any temple and speak with a priest.}
{1043}{I believe there is one in Tarant on the northern end of Lion's Head Circle.}
{1044}{When you have the means, travel to the village of Stillwater.}
{1045}{I will leave word with the InnKeeper at the Bleeding Rose Inn as to where you can find me.}
{1046}{Joachim}

{1050}{
Professor Thomas Eakins
Tarant University

}
{1051}{L'anamelach. This is bad news, indeed.}
{1052}{I have sent a copy of the Legend of T'erre d' V'nt, which should have all the information you may need to defeat the beast.}
{1053}{DO NOT attempt to fight the demon until you have read the information contained in this volume. To do so would insure a disastrous turn of events.}
{1054}{Good luck.}
{1055}{

Prof. Eakins}


